Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:50:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wave_lib_hdc: read the HDC time levels in order

The time-level logic of wave_prestep_fnpf/cfd had two bugs:
- continuous input (source P 45 2, the default) was read one record per
  step. At startup it read one record too far, and whenever a target step
  spans two source records it fell behind for good (NHFLOW -> NHFLOW:
  0.64 s behind after 20 s). Single files (P 45 1) were read correctly
  except for a stale first level at startup.
- the time search could read simtime[] past its end.

New wave_lib_hdc_time_levels.cpp: q1/q2 as before; each level is read
exactly once and in order, and a continuous file skips the records it
does not need. Continuous and single-file input now give bitwise the
same result (FNPF and NHFLOW targets).

Changes old input: FNPF -> FNPF nesting moves by about one source record.
The old read-ahead offset another delay of about one step: FNPF stamps
its state files and gauges with t^n but they hold t^n+1. Phase vs the
source gauges in fnpf_2d_hdc (900 steps): -0.007 s before, -0.030 s
after, same rms after shifting. What remains is about one target step
and does not grow.

